# React 19 form event types

On `react@19` / `@types/react@19.2+`, **`React.FormEvent` / `React.FormEventHandler` are deprecated** for submit flows. Use **`React.SubmitEvent<HTMLFormElement>`** (and `SubmitEventHandler`) — see `@types/react` deprecation on `FormEvent` and `HTMLAttributes.onSubmit` typing.

## Typing `onSubmit`

Use a **named** handler with `React.SubmitEvent<HTMLFormElement>`; avoid anonymous wrappers that split `preventDefault` from submit logic. **`useActionState` + `<form action>`** when the submit is a Server Action; keep a typed **`onSubmit`** for client SDK flows (e.g. `authClient.*`) — do not migrate those to `useActionState` only because it is newer.

```tsx
async function onSubmit(event: React.SubmitEvent<HTMLFormElement>) {
  event.preventDefault();
  // ...
}

<form onSubmit={onSubmit}>
```

`React.SyntheticEvent<HTMLFormElement>` is a weaker fallback; prefer **`SubmitEvent`**.
